---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import BusinessPerspectiveNote from '../../components/BusinessPerspectiveNote.astro';
import ToolNextStep from '../../components/ToolNextStep.astro';
import CourseProviderComparison from '../../components/CourseProviderComparison.astro';

const title = 'Course Provider Comparison: Check a Course Before Paying';
const description = 'Compare two or three course providers on recognition, full cost, practice and results, spot warning signs and send questions in writing. Free.';
const canonical = 'https://futurecareerschool.com/tools/course-provider-comparison/';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical}>
  <Nav activePage="tools" />
  <BusinessPerspectiveNote />
  <main>
    <section class="tool-hero container"><p class="eyebrow">FREE DUE-DILIGENCE TOOL</p><h1>Course Provider <span>Comparison</span></h1><p class="lead">Ask every provider the same questions before a deadline or a sales call turns doubt into a payment. Check two or three providers in one table, spot warning signs, and copy a message to send them in writing.</p><p class="tool-limits">This does not rank providers or check their claims for you. Use current official sources and written answers.</p></section>
    <section class="container tool-shell"><CourseProviderComparison /></section>
    <section class="container tool-explainer"><h2>What to compare</h2><div class="explainer-grid"><article><h3>Recognition</h3><p>Check who approves the course and what it leads to, such as a degree, a licence or only a certificate.</p></article><article><h3>Learning evidence</h3><p>Ask what learners make, who reviews it, and whether the feedback is specific enough to improve the work.</p></article><article><h3>Outcome claims</h3><p>Keep dated, comparable evidence apart from testimonials, guarantees and marketing words.</p></article></div>
    <h2>A worked example (an illustration, not a real provider)</h2><p>A family compares two data analytics courses. Provider A gives only a headline fee, says every learner gets a job, and wants payment today. Provider B sends the total fee and refund rule in writing and shows learner projects.</p><p>The tool marks Provider A as high risk because of the guarantee and the pressure, and Provider B as worth checking further. It does not say B is good. It says what to ask next and to check who approves the course.</p>
    <h2>When to talk to a person</h2><p>If the fee is a large part of the family's education money, talk to a counsellor or to someone who finished the course recently. Pay only to the institution's official account and keep the receipt.</p></section>
    <ToolNextStep toolName="Course Provider Comparison" audience="parent" />
  </main><Footer />
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .tool-hero{padding:5rem 1.25rem 2rem}.tool-hero h1{max-width:850px}.tool-hero h1 span{color:var(--gold,#e5b84a)}.lead{max-width:760px;font-size:1.15rem;line-height:1.7}.tool-limits{max-width:760px;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.6;color:var(--muted,#b9c2c1)}.tool-shell{max-width:1050px}.tool-explainer{padding:2rem 1.25rem 5rem}.tool-explainer h2{margin-top:0}.explainer-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1rem}.explainer-grid article{padding:1rem;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.14);border-radius:14px}.explainer-grid h3{margin-top:0}@media(max-width:720px){.tool-hero{padding-top:3rem}.explainer-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
